   "note": "2 x 8 at 2.54 mm, rows 15.24 mm apart, USB-C at the top. IO20 = RX, IO21 = TX, IO8 = SDA / LED, IO9 = SCL / BOOT. Two independent footprints agree on this order; they disagree by about 1 mm on where the pins sit along the board, so the outline is drawn with the pins centred. One maker's file (Elecrow) shows a different order and spacing: check your board's print. Castellated: with deadbug pads (Pads of this part > Deadbug) you can solder it flat on the copper, or Shift+M to mirror it so it sits on the copper side. "
